Doug Freyburger wrote:
> kanze wrote:

> > Just how bad is the penalty for body armor for a monk?

> It greatly depends on how you view the monk character class.

> 1) If you view the monk as a Grand Master martial arts
> fighter, the penalty is -20.  Easily overcome with maxed out
> luck strength and dexterity.

> 2) If you view the monk as a spellcaster as adaptible as a
> wizard but with lower max skills and for weapons mostly a
> blank slate that is filled in as artifacts arrive, the penalty
> is near zero.

> > I've currently got a monk who stumbled upon GDSM.

> Since DSM does not interfere with spell casting then head
> down path #2.

That was my original intent, to begin with.  A crossbow and some
bolts for ranged attacts, until I got the spells going, but to
mainly depend on spells.  The RNG had other ideas, however: no
attack spells before the castle, and a gift of Snickersee.

> > Wielding a +7 Snickersee---I know that Monks aren't
> > supposed to do that, but I since my god was nice enough to give
> > it to me...  And obviously, basic in long sword, and not going
> > to get any better.  (I didn't think monks could use weapons
> > effectively, but this one seems to be able to.)

> But getting a gift unrestricts its weapon class and a good
> artifact with maxed luck strength and dexterity never misses
> and most hit harder than a Grand Master kick.

Quite.  And unrestricted in long sword means that I can also use
the enchanted Excalibur that I found in a bones file.

On the other hand, I've found that some of the spells I could
never use (until much later, at least) as a Samurai or a
Valkyrie are quite handy now.  Sleep (which I had from the
start) got me out of trouble more than once at the beginning,
and now that I've got a robe and a helm of intelligence, I'm at
0% failure for most of what I know, even without dropping my
small shield.

So I started experimenting with spells I'd never used before,
and now have a pet rock troll (and a lot less shopkeepers,
guards and priests).

> > I've got a fair number of blank scrolls, and two unused
> > magic markers, so if the GDSM isn't going to hurt my
> > fighting ability that much, I'll enchant it up...

> It will not effect playing style #2 at all.  With maxed luck the
> only effect playing style #1 is an unending stream of extra
> messages when you fight.

Which means I can effectively use both, depending on where I am,
and who else is there.

